[1] AP-tail two-clock theorem
  scanned_m=13..400
  counts={'ap_boundary': 1, 'q13_puncture': 358, 'fixed_point_tail': 29}
  non_strict_except_AP=0
  min_strict_margin=1/378
    min_margin_row m=26 kind=fixed_point_tail t=2/27 height=2/27
  proof:
    If 13 does not divide m, t=1/13 gives every speed a nonzero
    residue mod 13, hence distance at least 1/13 > 1/14.
    If m=13s and s>=2, t=s/(13s+1) makes runners 1 and m
    bind at distance t.  For 2<=j<=12 in the AP core, the
    distance is j*t or 1-j*t, and both are at least t; moreover
    t>1/14 exactly when s>1.  The single exception s=1 is AP.

